## What this means in practice for Hanarr

- You can download, install, and run Hanarr for your own personal job search -- searching for
  postings, tracking your own applications, and preparing your own application materials.
- Any other use -- for a business, nonprofit, school, government agency, someone else's job
  search, or anything unrelated to your own personal job search -- is **not permitted** without
  the copyright holder's express prior permission.
- You **cannot** modify Hanarr, create derivative works from it, or distribute copies of it
  (modified or not, in whole or in part) to anyone else, regardless of purpose -- this includes
  rewriting or reimplementing it based on having studied the code, not just copy-pasting it.
- You **cannot** remove or alter the copyright/attribution notice, claim authorship of it or any
  part of it, or use the "Hanarr" name or branding on anything else, including a fork, rebrand,
  or competing product.
- Only the copyright holder (David Hunsicker) may modify, redistribute, or sell this software,
  or grant broader licenses to others.

This summary is provided for convenience only and is not part of the license; the license text
above is what actually governs.

