## A note on what a license can and can't do

This license gives the copyright holder legal grounds -- a copyright infringement claim, a DMCA
takedown request, a cease-and-desist -- against anyone who violates it. It cannot technically
prevent someone with access to the source from copying it in the first place; no license text
can. If the GitHub repository stays public, anyone can view and clone the code regardless of what
this file says -- the license only controls what they're legally permitted to *do* with it
afterward, and gives grounds to act once they don't. The only way to reduce that exposure directly
is to restrict who can see the source at all (e.g. a private repository).
